# Full-bleed card images

Card photos must touch all four edges of the media area. Fix **layout CSS and source assets** — `object-cover` alone cannot fix padded image files.

## Required layout

```tsx
<article className="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl">
  <div className="aspect-square overflow-hidden bg-muted">
    <img
      src={item.image}
      alt={item.title}
      className="block h-full w-full object-cover"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </div>
  <div className="p-3">{/* text */}</div>
</article>
```

| Element | Classes / styles |
|---------|------------------|
| Card | `overflow-hidden` when corners are rounded |
| Media wrapper | `aspect-square` or `aspect-video` + `overflow-hidden` |
| Image | `block h-full w-full object-cover` |

## Avoid

- `object-contain` on card hero images (shows gaps)
- Fixed `width`/`height` on `<img>` without a sized parent
- Assuming CDN `fit=crop` means the file is full-bleed — verify the saved asset

## When CSS is correct but the photo still looks tiny

The JPG/PNG likely has baked-in white/black padding (common with Scene7/CDN assets). Trim or re-fetch the asset; do not add more CSS.

| Symptom | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| Small photo in colored square | Trim or re-fetch padded source file |
| Thin gap below image | Add `block` on `<img>` |
| Image past rounded corners | Add `overflow-hidden` on card and wrapper |

Before finishing, visually confirm at least two cards and hard-refresh if assets changed.
